hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15939","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said, Abu Na'ama al-Adawi narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Budayl, from Iyas ibn Zuhayr, from Suwayd ibn Hubayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best wealth of a man for him is a productive mare or a pollinated iron share. And Rawh said in his house, and it was said to him: You told us: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
